    "body": "Small fixes to stale argument metadata and help text in the wallet RPCs, split into five focused commits (per l0rinc's review):\n\n1. `5fcbbf8` — **listtransactions**: the \"Negative from\" error references the skip argument by its old name\n2. `9aa8977` — **listsinceblock**: name the failing argument when target_confirmations < 1 instead of a bare \"Invalid parameter\"\n3. `f214b2c` — **sendmany**: the help examples pass values in the ignored minconf position; describe what the example actually sets and pass null for the placeholder\n4. `3a2a982` — **getbalance**: add the (DEPRECATED) marker to include_watchonly, matching the identical argument in six other RPCs\n5. `f6f5c4e` — **send**: include_watching used a string default \"false\" on a BOOL argument, rendering as default=\"false\" in the help; adds help metadata coverage in wallet_send\n\nEach commit is self-contained and green individually (the required test updates travel with their code change).",
